! Art Sigils — Example Zero Inscription

The following source alone carries the portable inscription. Copy both the native TW5 definition and its call, with the blank separator; exclude this meme wrapper. The entire transmitted source occupies **999 characters**, including its line breaks; a 1,024-character ceiling serves as a portability *target*, not an ideal length.

```tiddlywiki
\procedure art-sigil(worktype:"artwork" subject read imagery:"follow subject and read" treatment:"suit the read" composition:"serve the read" relation:"where meaningful" depiction-scope:"follow worktype and imagery") <<worktype>>: <<subject>>. Read: <<read>>. Imagery: <<imagery>>. Treatment: <<treatment>>. Composition: <<composition>>. Relation: <<relation>>. Depiction scope: <<depiction-scope>>.

<<art-sigil worktype:"concept-art pinboard" subject:"shattered Olympos, Rift of Tempes, Phlegra" read:"artists dispute a passable mountain route" imagery:"luminous relief panorama; vellum route correction; charcoal relic; green refuge" treatment:"Heinrich Berann panorama; Bernhard Jenny shaded relief; Luka Rejec exploratory mythpunk; Piranesi/Ian Miller only in dark Phlegra; distinct papers" composition:"dominant panorama, smaller pinned studies" relation:"saddle correction refutes painted pass; bone or machine?" depiction-scope:"board only; figures in studies; artist labels/photos unseen">>
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bounds>>
!! Reading, artist basins and representational boundaries

* Supplied `subject` and `read` hold the governing intention. The now-explicit `composition` keeps the large landscape and smaller pinned studies in view; `relation` preserves the route correction and the unresolved relic.
* Five deliberately scoped *direct named artist references* guide different tasks: **Heinrich Berann** (panoramic landforms), **Bernhard Jenny** (shaded terrain relief), **Luka Rejec** (explorable mythpunk), **Piranesi** and **Ian Miller** (Phlegra's dark, ruinous and organic-mechanical studies only). These names cue overlapping visual traditions, not guaranteed model behavior or authorization to reproduce a particular work.
* The broader register stays available in the Folio. Tom Patterson, Eduard Imhof and Erwin Raisz remain represented through relief and terrain vocabulary; Moebius through luminous open space; Doré through scale and value; Kilian Eng through localized anomalous color. No additional proper names enter this self-contained Inscription.
* Explicit depiction-scope keeps the board as the outer image, human figures inside depicted studies, and artist credits and source photographs outside the picture. The individual artwork and style references must not become literal paper labels.
* The real Olympus relief, aerial and embodied photographs remain external references in the companion Folio; an AI cannot retrieve those URLs without appropriate access or attached imagery.
* The complete native TW5 procedure is included unchanged from `art-sigils-procedures.mem`. Its defaults remain available for future Inscription forms; the present call states the most consequential composition and relation choices directly.
<<~/ahu>>
